      "message": "perf(app): walk the selection once per input for the page\n\nThe Geometry tab asked operation::selection_account and the Contour\nfields asked operation::contour_auto_side on each frame. Each ask ran\nthe full selection walk again: 4.2 ms and 4.1 ms per still frame in\nrelease on fig8 with ten top chains (#2238 probe, state b).\n\nThe new operation/selection_memo.rs keeps one memo entry per input:\nthe setup, the picks and the parameters by value, and each world read\nof the walk (facet allocation, pose, setup alignment, setup definition,\nmachine kind, WCS pose and word, document unit). One miss runs the walk\none time and keeps the notes, the door refusal and the Auto side.\n\nGeneration, the pick doors and the region walk do not read this memo.\nThey walk for themselves, so the side that the toolpath uses does not\nchange.\n\nPinned by contour_side_and_account_walk_once_per_input (every hit\nequals a fresh walk, across picks, undo, a side edit and a part move)\nand by the frame-cost probe (selections = 0 on still frames).\n\nFixes #2248\nFixes #2249\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
